<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Credit Memorandum — South River Capital — {{ name }}</title>
<style>
:root{--navy:#0f2a43;--navy-2:#1c3d5a;--gold:#b9952b;--ink:#1a1a1a;--ink-soft:#444;--rule:#cdd3da;--rule-strong:#9aa6b2;--paper:#fff;--desk:#e9e7e0;--zebra:#f4f6f8;}
*{box-sizing:border-box;}html,body{margin:0;padding:0;}
body{background:var(--desk);font-family:"Times New Roman",Times,serif;font-size:10pt;line-height:1.42;color:var(--ink);-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;padding:32px 16px 64px;}
.page{width:8.5in;min-height:11in;background:var(--paper);margin:0 auto 28px;padding:.7in .75in .85in;box-shadow:0 2px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.12);border-radius:2px;position:relative;}
p{margin:0 0 7pt;text-wrap:pretty;}.lead{margin-bottom:9pt;}strong{font-weight:bold;}
.section{margin-top:16pt;}.section:first-of-type{margin-top:0;}
h2.sec{font-size:11.5pt;font-weight:bold;color:#000;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;margin:0 0 8pt;padding-bottom:4pt;border-bottom:1.5pt solid var(--navy);display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8pt;}
h2.sec .num{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;color:#fff;background:var(--navy);padding:2pt 5pt;letter-spacing:.05em;transform:translateY(-1pt);}
h3.sub{font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;color:#000;margin:11pt 0 4pt;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.03em;}
.masthead{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;border-bottom:3px solid var(--navy);padding-bottom:10pt;margin-bottom:4pt;}
.brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;}.brand .brand-logo{height:50px;width:auto;display:block;background:#fff;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:4px;}
.brand .wm{line-height:1;}.brand .wm .name{font-size:16pt;font-weight:bold;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;}
.brand .wm .tag{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:6.5pt;letter-spacing:.32em;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:4px;font-weight:bold;}
.doc-meta{text-align:right;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;}
.doc-meta .conf{font-size:7pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#fff;background:var(--gold);padding:2pt 6pt;display:inline-block;text-transform:uppercase;}
.doc-meta .dt{font-size:8pt;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:6pt;}.doc-meta .dt span{color:var(--ink);font-weight:bold;}
.doc-title{text-align:center;margin:14pt 0 16pt;}.doc-title .kicker{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7.5pt;letter-spacing:.4em;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:bold;}
.doc-title h1{font-size:21pt;font-weight:bold;color:#000;letter-spacing:.04em;margin:5pt 0 0;text-transform:uppercase;}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:4pt 0 6pt;font-size:9.5pt;}
caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;color:#000;padding-bottom:3pt;font-size:9.5pt;}
th,td{border:.75pt solid var(--rule);padding:3.5pt 7pt;vertical-align:top;text-align:left;}
thead th{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7.5pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;border-color:var(--navy-2);}
table.kv td.k{width:30%;background:#f1f4f7;font-weight:bold;color:#000;white-space:nowrap;}
table.kv.two td.k{width:22%;}
.num-col{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap;}
tbody tr.total td{font-weight:bold;background:#eef1f4;border-top:1.25pt solid var(--rule-strong);}
tbody tr.grand td{font-weight:bold;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border-color:var(--navy-2);}
.zebra tbody tr:nth-child(even) td{background:var(--zebra);}
/* In zebra tables the even-row stripe outranks tr.grand's navy background (equal
   specificity, later rule), leaving white text on a light stripe whenever the
   grand row lands on an even index. Re-assert the navy band at higher specificity
   so the Net Cash Flow row always matches the other grand rows
   (Lauren, 2026-07-28). Literal colors, not var(), so the row also survives
   Word's HTML engine (which drops var() backgrounds — see render_word). */
.zebra tbody tr.grand td{background:#0f2a43;color:#fff;border-color:#1c3d5a;}
.src-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:9pt;margin-top:8pt;}
.src{border:.75pt solid var(--rule);border-top:2.5pt solid var(--navy);padding:7pt 9pt;background:#fafbfc;}
.src .lab{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7pt;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:bold;color:#000;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4pt;}
.src .ord{font-size:8pt;color:#000;font-weight:bold;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;margin-bottom:2pt;}
.callout{border-left:3pt solid #000;background:#fcfbf6;padding:9pt 12pt;margin:6pt 0 8pt;}
ul.tight{margin:3pt 0 7pt;padding-left:18pt;}ul.tight li{margin-bottom:3pt;}
.faq{margin-bottom:9pt;}.faq .q{font-weight:bold;color:#000;margin-bottom:2pt;}
.note-fine{font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--ink-soft);}
.pg-footer{position:absolute;left:.75in;right:.75in;bottom:.42in;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:6.8pt;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8a8a;text-transform:uppercase;border-top:.75pt solid var(--rule);padding-top:5pt;}
/* The compliance checklist, now the closing APPENDIX. Literal colors on the
   status boxes (not var()) so they survive Word's HTML engine — see render_word. */
.cover-title{margin:8pt 0 8pt;}
.cover-title h1{font-size:17pt;}
.cover-sec{margin-top:9pt;}
.cover-sec h2.sec{margin-bottom:5pt;}
.cover-sec h3.sub{margin-top:0;}
/* Rule 15 — each financed debt listed under the summary liability it rolls into: indented, lighter, and hairline-ruled so it reads as a breakdown of the line above rather than another liability. */tbody tr.dsc td{background:#fbfcfd;font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--ink-soft);border-top-width:.4pt;border-top-style:dotted;padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;}tbody tr.dsc td.dsc-lbl{padding-left:26pt;}.dsc-note{display:block;font-size:7.5pt;color:#6b7683;}table.compliance{font-size:8pt;line-height:1.25;margin:2pt 0 4pt;}
table.compliance td{padding:2pt 5pt;}
table.compliance thead th{font-size:7pt;padding:2.5pt 5pt;}
.st-cell{white-space:nowrap;}
.st{display:inline-block;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:6.5pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9aa6b2;border:.75pt solid #cdd3da;background:#fff;padding:1pt 4pt;margin-right:3pt;}
.st:last-child{margin-right:0;}
.st.on{background:#0f2a43;border-color:#1c3d5a;color:#fff;}
.cover-sec .callout{padding:6pt 10pt;margin:3pt 0 4pt;font-size:8.5pt;}
.approval{display:flex;gap:24pt;margin-top:10pt;break-inside:avoid;}
.approval .sig{flex:1;}
.approval .sig-date{flex:0 0 1.5in;}
.approval .line{border-bottom:1pt solid #1a1a1a;height:14pt;}
.approval .cap{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#444;margin-top:3pt;}
@page{size:letter;margin:.7in .75in .6in;}
.kpi-strip{display:flex;gap:0;margin:10pt 0 4pt;border-top:1.5pt solid var(--navy);border-bottom:.75pt solid var(--rule);}
.kpi{flex:1;padding:7pt 10pt 7pt 0;}
.kpi + .kpi{padding-left:12pt;border-left:.75pt solid var(--rule);}
.kpi .v{font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:15pt;font-weight:bold;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.1;}
.kpi .k{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:6.5pt;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a8a8a;margin-top:3pt;}
.meta-line{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:8pt;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#6a6a6a;text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:4pt;}
.risk-item{margin:0 0 7pt;}
.risk-item .rl{font-weight:bold;color:var(--navy);}
.risk-item .rm{display:block;margin-top:2pt;padding-left:10pt;border-left:2pt solid var(--gold);}
.risk-item .open{display:block;margin-top:2pt;padding-left:10pt;border-left:2pt solid #b00;color:#b00;font-style:italic;}
.tbd{color:#8a6a00;font-style:italic;}
@media print{body{background:none;padding:0;}.page{width:auto;min-height:0;margin:0;padding:0;box-shadow:none;border-radius:0;break-after:page;}.page:last-child{break-after:auto;}.pg-footer{display:none;}.section,.faq,.src,.callout,tr,thead{break-inside:avoid;}h2.sec,h3.sub{break-after:avoid;}th,td,thead th,tbody tr.grand td,.brand .brand-logo,.doc-meta .conf,h2.sec .num,.src,.st{-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;}}
</style></head>
<body style="background-color:rgba(255,255,253,0.98)">
{%- set pg = namespace(n=0) -%}
{%- set total_pages = page_count -%}
{% macro footer() %}{% set pg.n = pg.n + 1 %}<div class="pg-footer"><span>South River Capital &mdash; Confidential &mdash; {{ name }} Credit Memorandum</span><span>Page {{ pg.n }} of {{ total_pages }}</span></div>{% endmacro %}

<div class="page">
<header class="masthead"><div class="brand"><img class="brand-logo" src="{{ logo }}" alt="South River Capital"></div><div class="doc-meta"><div class="conf">Confidential</div><div class="dt">Memo Date: <span>{{ md_fmt }}</span></div></div></header>

<div class="doc-title"><div class="kicker">Credit Memorandum &nbsp;|&nbsp; Confidential</div><h1>{{ headline }}</h1></div>
<p class="meta-line">{{ md_long }}{% if asset_class %} &nbsp;|&nbsp; {{ asset_class }}{% endif %}{% if purpose %} &nbsp;|&nbsp; {{ purpose }}{% endif %}</p>

<div class="kpi-strip">
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ loan_money }}</div><div class="k">Loan Amount</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ rate }}%{% if fee %} + {{ fee }} pt{% if fee != '1' %}s{% endif %}{% endif %}</div><div class="k">Rate / Points</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{% if ltv %}{{ ltv }}%{% else %}{{ lti }}%{% endif %}</div><div class="k">{% if ltv %}Loan-to-Value{% else %}Loan-to-Income{% endif %}</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ months }} mo</div><div class="k">{% if is_io %}Interest Only{% else %}Amortizing{% endif %}</div></div>
</div>

<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Executive Summary</h2>
<div class="callout"><p>{{ exec_summary }}</p></div></section>

{{ footer() }}
</div>

<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Loan Summary</h2>
<table class="kv"><tbody>
<tr><td class="k">Borrower</td><td>{{ name }}</td></tr>
{% if property_owner %}<tr><td class="k">Property Owner / Grantor</td><td>{{ property_owner }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
<tr><td class="k">Guarantor(s)</td><td>{{ guarantors }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Purpose</td><td>{{ purpose or tbd }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Loan Amount</td><td>{{ loan_money }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Term</td><td>{{ months }} months{% if mat_fmt %} &mdash; matures {{ mat_fmt }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Interest Rate</td><td>{{ rate }}% fixed</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Origination</td><td>{{ fee }}% ({{ fee_amt }})</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Payments</td><td>{{ payments_desc }}</td></tr>
{% if show_investor %}<tr><td class="k">Investor Return</td><td>{{ investor.rate }}% and {{ investor.points }} point{% if investor.points != '1' %}s{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
<tr><td class="k">Collateral</td><td>{{ collateral_cell }}</td></tr>
{% if collateral_money %}<tr><td class="k">Collateral Value</td><td>{{ collateral_money }}{% if collateral_basis %} &mdash; {{ collateral_basis }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Loan-to-Value</td><td>{{ ltv }}%</td></tr>{% endif %}
{# The LTI basis has to be disclosed, not just used: a reader cannot check the
   ratio without knowing which income figure it ran on. #}
<tr><td class="k">{% if contracted_money %}Contracted Income (facility term){% else %}Qualifying Income (annual){% endif %}</td><td>{{ income_basis_money }}{% if contracted_money %} committed by contract or lease{% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Loan-to-Income</td><td>{{ lti }}%</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Prepayment</td><td>{{ prepayment or tbd }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Key Conditions</td><td>{{ key_conditions or tbd }}</td></tr>
</tbody></table></section>
{{ footer() }}
</div>

<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Collateral Analysis</h2>
{% if collateral_notes %}<p>{{ collateral_notes }}</p>
{% elif collateral_money %}<p>The facility is secured by {{ collateral_desc or 'the pledged collateral' }}, valued at <strong>{{ collateral_money }}</strong>. A first-lien position is perfected by UCC-1 filing and, for real property, a recorded mortgage or deed of trust. <span class="tbd">[Describe the collateral: what it is, its condition, the valuation basis and date, and who prepared it.]</span></p>
{% else %}<p>No specific collateral is pledged. The facility is unsecured and rests on the full personal guarantee of the Borrower, supported by a UCC-1 filing against the Borrower's business assets.</p>{% endif %}

{% if coverage.rows %}
<table class="zebra"><thead><tr><th>Collateral Coverage</th><th class="num-col">Value</th><th class="num-col">LTV</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in coverage.rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.basis }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ r.value_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{% if r.ltv %}{{ r.ltv }}%{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
{% if coverage.equity_money %}<tr class="total"><td>Equity cushion below SRC's position</td><td class="num-col">{{ coverage.equity_money }}</td><td class="num-col">&mdash;</td></tr>{% endif %}
</tbody></table>
<p class="note-fine">Each basis is shown with the leverage it implies, including the unfavourable ones, so the reader sees the LTV under a stressed value and not only under the appraisal.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Borrower Profile</h2>
<p class="lead">{{ background_text }}</p></section>
{{ footer() }}
</div>

<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Financial Analysis</h2>
{% if financial_notes %}<p>{{ financial_notes }}</p>{% endif %}
{% if fin.periods %}
<table class="zebra"><thead><tr><th></th>{% for p in fin.periods %}<th class="num-col">{{ p.period }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Revenue</td>{% for p in fin.periods %}<td class="num-col">{{ p.revenue_money }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
<tr><td>EBITDA</td>{% for p in fin.periods %}<td class="num-col">{{ p.ebitda_money }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
<tr><td>Net Income</td>{% for p in fin.periods %}<td class="num-col">{{ p.net_income_money }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
<tr><td>Proposed Debt Service</td>{% for p in fin.periods %}<td class="num-col">{{ p.debt_service_money }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
<tr class="total"><td>DSCR (EBITDA / Debt Service)</td>{% for p in fin.periods %}<td class="num-col">{{ p.dscr_fmt }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
</tbody></table>
{% else %}
<p class="tbd">[No financial statements were among the documents. Request FY statements and YTD interims, then re-run the extraction: Revenue, EBITDA, Net Income and DSCR per period populate this table.]</p>
{% endif %}
<p>Annual debt service on the proposed facility is <strong>{{ debt_service_money }}</strong>. Break-even EBITDA is {{ fin.breakeven[0].money }} for 1.00x coverage, {{ fin.breakeven[1].money }} for 1.25x, and {{ fin.breakeven[2].money }} for 1.50x.</p>
</section>

{% if has_pfs %}
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Guarantor Cash Flow</h2>
<p>The analysis below is based on the Borrower's documented income and the Personal Financial Statement on file. After servicing all existing debt, the Borrower maintains the net cash flow shown below.</p>
<table class="zebra"><caption>Personal Cash Flow Analysis &mdash; {{ name }}</caption><thead><tr><th style="width:34px">Note</th><th>Line Item</th><th class="num-col">Annual</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ cf_html }}</tbody></table>
<p class="note-fine"><strong>Notes:</strong>&nbsp; 1 &mdash; Annual qualifying income, documented and recurring. &nbsp;2 &mdash; Other income per Annual Income section of PFS. &nbsp;3 &mdash; Estimated 45% blended tax rate applied to gross income. &nbsp;4 &mdash; Estimated 10% of gross income to cover all ordinary living expenses. &nbsp;5 &mdash; Proposed Facility shown at principal; the interest-included total is carried as a liability on the Personal Financial Statement.</p></section>
{% endif %}
{{ footer() }}
</div>

{% if has_pfs %}
<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Personal Financial Statement</h2>
<table><caption>As reported on Personal Financial Statement &mdash; {{ name }}</caption><thead><tr><th>Assets</th><th class="num-col">Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ pfs_html }}</tbody></table>
<p><strong>Credit:</strong> {{ credit_text }}</p></section>
{{ footer() }}
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Risk Considerations &amp; Mitigants</h2>
{% if risks %}
{% for r in risks %}<div class="risk-item"><span class="rl">{{ r.risk }}:</span> {{ r.detail }}{% if r.mitigant %}<span class="rm"><strong>Mitigant:</strong> {{ r.mitigant }}</span>{% else %}<span class="open"><strong>Mitigant:</strong> none identified &mdash; outstanding at the date of this memorandum.</span>{% endif %}</div>{% endfor %}
{% else %}
<p class="tbd">[No risks were captured from the documents. State each material risk and the mitigant that answers it &mdash; an unmitigated risk still belongs here.]</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">How will the borrower reservice the debt</h2>
<p><strong>Primary Repayment source:</strong> {{ repay_primary }}</p>
<p><strong>Secondary Repayment source:</strong> {{ repay_secondary }}</p>
<p><strong>Tertiary Repayment source:</strong> {{ repay_tertiary }}</p></section>
{{ footer() }}
</div>

<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Sources and Uses Summary</h2>
<p>Estimated use of loan proceeds are below.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Disbursement</th><th class="num-col">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ uses_html }}</tbody></table>
<p class="note-fine">Disbursement amounts are estimates sourced from the deal documents; confirm against the final settlement statement.</p></section>

<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Repayment Schedule</h2>
<p>{{ repayment_intro }}</p>
{% if repayment_bands %}
<table class="zebra"><thead><tr><th>Period</th><th class="num-col">Interest</th><th class="num-col">Principal</th><th class="num-col">Total Paid</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for b in repayment_bands %}<tr><td>{{ b.label }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ b.interest_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ b.principal_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ b.total_money }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
<tr class="total"><td>Total</td><td class="num-col">{{ repayment_totals.interest_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ repayment_totals.principal_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ repayment_totals.total_money }}</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p class="note-fine">Annual bands; the payment-by-payment schedule is Exhibit A to the promissory note.</p>
{% else %}
<table class="zebra"><thead><tr><th style="width:52px">Payment</th><th>Date</th><th class="num-col">Interest</th><th class="num-col">Principal</th><th class="num-col">Total</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ repayment_html }}</tbody></table>
{% endif %}
</section>
{{ footer() }}
</div>

<div class="page">
{% if show_investor %}
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Investor Returns</h2>
<p>Investors receive {{ investor.rate }}% per annum, paid monthly, plus {{ investor.points }} point{% if investor.points != '1' %}s{% endif %} at closing.{% if investor_differs %} These are the investor economics and differ from what the Borrower pays ({{ rate }}% and {{ fee }} points).{% else %} These are the same economics the Borrower pays.{% endif %}</p>
<table class="zebra"><thead><tr><th></th><th class="num-col">Per {{ investor.unit_money }} Invested</th><th class="num-col">Full {{ loan_money }}</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Points at closing ({{ investor.points }}%)</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.per_unit.points_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.full.points_money }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Monthly interest</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.per_unit.monthly_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.full.monthly_money }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Annual interest ({{ investor.rate }}%)</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.per_unit.annual_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.full.annual_money }}</td></tr>
<tr class="total"><td>Total income over {{ months }} months</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.per_unit.total_money }}</td><td class="num-col">{{ investor.full.total_money }}</td></tr>
</tbody></table></section>
{% endif %}

<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Required Documents</h2>
{% if required_documents %}
<ul class="tight">{% for d in required_documents %}<li>{{ d }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% else %}
<p class="tbd">[List what must be in hand before closing &mdash; valuations, entity documents, title, insurance, payoff letters, financial statements.]</p>
{% endif %}
{% if doc_list_html %}<h3 class="sub">Documents reviewed</h3>
<table class="kv"><tbody>{{ doc_list_html }}</tbody></table>{% endif %}
</section>

<section class="section"><h2 class="sec">Recommendation</h2>
<div class="callout"><p>{{ recommendation }}</p></div>
<div class="approval" style="margin-top:14pt">
  <div class="sig"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Prepared by</div></div>
  <div class="sig sig-date"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Date</div></div>
</div>
<div class="approval">
  <div class="sig"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Reviewed by</div></div>
  <div class="sig sig-date"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Date</div></div>
</div>
<div class="approval">
  <div class="sig"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Approved by</div></div>
  <div class="sig sig-date"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Date</div></div>
</div>
</section>
<p class="note-fine" style="margin-top:12pt">This memorandum is prepared solely for the internal credit evaluation of South River Capital and its participation lenders. All information is derived from executed loan documents, third-party reports, and borrower-provided financial statements on file. This document is <strong>confidential</strong> and intended only for authorized recipients.</p>
{{ footer() }}
</div>

{% if show_compliance %}
<div class="page">
<div class="doc-title cover-title"><div class="kicker">Appendix</div><h1>Policy Compliance</h1></div>
<section class="section cover-sec">
<table class="zebra compliance"><thead><tr><th>Criteria / Covenant</th><th style="width:78px">Requirement</th><th>Actual</th><th style="width:104px">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ compliance_html }}</tbody></table></section>
<section class="section cover-sec"><h3 class="sub">Exceptions &amp; Mitigants</h3>
<div class="callout">{{ exceptions_html }}</div></section>
